Use in ZeroJ
------------

The vectors are test data only. ZeroJ's tests read them to check its transcript layer (the
SHAKE128 duplex sponge, its codecs and the sigma-proofs_Shake128_BLS12381 encodings) against the
drafts (ADR-0061, invariant I12; docs/specs/bulletproof-range-bls12-381-g1-v1.md section 10). The
zeroj-test-vectors module is never published, so these files are not part of any ZeroJ release
artifact.
